---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { release, site, sourceUrl } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Roadmap" description="Released capabilities, current engineering work and future proposals, with public source links and no invented shipping commitments.">
  <div class="container"><header class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Direction / Not a release promise</span><h1>Built in the open.<br />Labeled honestly.</h1><p class="lead">Published releases tell you what is available. Issues and design records explain what is being explored, implemented or validated. They are not interchangeable.</p></header>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Available now.</h2><p>The verified stable release is <a href={release.latest.url}>{release.latest.tag}</a>. Physical-terminal acceptance for this release remains pending.</p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Released</span><div><h3>Shell interaction and continuity</h3><p>Persistent zsh/Bash/Fish sessions, composer layouts, semantic highlighting, transcript tools and live-session resume.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/features/">Product capabilities <span>→</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Released</span><div><h3>Context, themes and first-slice workspaces</h3><p>Context Engine platform, declarative local packs, Status Strip 2.0, managed Claude Code, Theme Bridge, worktree management and read-only GitHub inspection. Each has specific boundaries—not blanket support for every extension or remote action.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/releases/">Release evidence <span>→</span></a></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Engineering in progress.</h2><p>Development and release-stabilization work is not promoted to stable by appearing on a branch. Current status lives in the linked issues and public Project.</p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">In development</span><div><h3>Execution interaction and output workflows</h3><p>The terminal workflow initiative explores making one command's result more useful for the next: output references, comparisons, diagnostic reports and command-queue interaction. These are not advertised as stable capabilities here.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href={`${site.repo}/issues/359`}>Terminal workflow initiative · #359 <span>↗</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Ongoing</span><div><h3>Native modules and trustworthy context</h3><p>The released foundation continues into module ecosystem work, observability and capability coverage. Executable extensions and remote pack trust are separate future security questions.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/305`}>Native modules · #305 <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/365`}>Observability · #365 <span>↗</span></a></div></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Validation pending</span><div><h3>Real hosts, real compatibility</h3><p>Latest-release physical QA, Linux/WSL 2 and additional terminal hosts need evidence from actual use. Passing CI is not the same as physical acceptance.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/docs/reference/physical-qa/">Release QA checklist <span>→</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/311`}>Linux and WSL 2 · #311 <span>↗</span></a></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Future proposals.</h2><p>Directions worth investigating, not scheduled commitments. Scope, feasibility, security and design approval can change what eventually ships.</p></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Planned · Future</span><div><h3>Learn the command line by doing</h3><p>Guided Bash/zsh lessons, practice files, helpful feedback and resumable progress. Strong real-shell isolation must be verified, or execution must be explicitly simulated or disabled.</p><a class="text-link spaced" href="/learn/">Explore future Learn Mode <span>→</span></a></div></div><div class="roadmap-item"><span class="badge">Research / proposal</span><div><h3>Broader integrations, without blurred authority</h3><p>Additional managed-agent adapters, workflow tool integrations and stronger isolation for executable mods require independent capability and security evidence.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/339`}>Agent adapters · #339 <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repo}/issues/341`}>Executable-mod isolation · #341 <span>↗</span></a></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="section"><aside class="note"><strong>A curated map, not every issue as a promise.</strong><p>Snapshot reviewed {release.verifiedAt}. See the <a href={sourceUrl('ROADMAP.md')}>release-pinned roadmap</a>, <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`}>live issues</a> and <a href="https://github.com/users/raiseCatError/projects/1">development Project</a> for the authoritative context. No dates or future version commitments are made here.</p></aside></section>
  </div>
</Base>
